<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo noupdate="0">
    <!-- Workforce section. Visible to every internal user (the cockpit shows a
         friendly empty-state when the user has no direct reports); managers see
         their queue.

         RENAMED by Workforce P1b: "My Team" -> "Team Approvals", icon `inbox`,
         and moved from the top of the rail (5) to 70. The name now says what
         the surface is FOR — it is the manager's decision queue, not a
         directory — and the rail reads as the week's loop with the queue near
         its end rather than as an org chart at its top. Label/icon/sequence
         only; the cockpit, its action and its gate are untouched.

         WHY "Team Approvals" AND NOT THE HANDOVER'S "Approvals":
         `pb_sidebar.item_approvals` already exists, labelled exactly
         "Approvals", in the OVERVIEW section (action tag `pb_approval`,
         `match_models` hr.payslip.run) — it is the PAYROLL approval cockpit,
         gated to the payroll approver tiers. Shipping the literal label would
         have put two identically-named entries on one rail, pointing at two
         different cockpits in two different domains: payslip-run approval
         versus a manager's own team's overtime/leave/trip requests. The one
         extra word keeps the rename's whole point (a decision queue, not an
         org chart) and removes an ambiguity a user would hit on their first
         day. Flagged in the P1b report for the owner to overrule — the
         alternative fix, renaming the payroll one to "Payroll Approvals", is
         the better long-term answer but belongs to whoever owns Overview. -->
    <!-- RETIRED by Workforce P3a: the queue is now the Approvals LENS of Mission
         Control (pb_mission mounts this component with embedded="true", W17).
         The action survives; only the rail entry goes, into the 900 band (W18).

         The lens is labelled plainly "Approvals" inside the shell. W28's
         uniqueness rule is about the `pb.sidebar.item` TABLE — where
         `pb_sidebar.item_approvals` (the payroll payslip-run cockpit) still owns
         that word — and the shell's lens rail is not that table. Inside a
         Workforce workspace there is exactly one approvals surface, so the
         disambiguating word this RECORD needs would only be noise there. -->
    <record id="item_my_team" model="pb.sidebar.item">
        <field name="section_id" ref="pb_sidebar.sec_workforce"/>
        <field name="name">Team Approvals</field>
        <field name="icon">inbox</field>
        <field name="sequence">912</field>
        <field name="active" eval="False"/>
        <field name="action_xmlid">pb_team.action_pb_team</field>
        <field name="action_tag">pb_team</field>
        <field name="match_action_tags">pb_team</field>
    </record>
</odoo>
